Description: Calculate sample sizes and statistical power for clinical and
    epidemiological study designs, including randomised trials,
    observational studies, diagnostic accuracy studies, and precision-based
    estimation. A unified interface covers superiority, non-inferiority,
    equivalence, paired and cluster designs, two-stage phase II trials,
    and bioequivalence. Results include the formula, calculation steps,
    parameter definitions, and methodological references. Implemented
    methods include diagnostic accuracy planning described by
    Hajian-Tilaki (2014) <doi:10.1016/j.jbi.2014.02.013>, survival study
    planning by Schoenfeld (1983) <doi:10.2307/2531021>, and exact
    single-stage phase II designs by A'Hern (2001) <doi:10.1002/sim.721>.
